
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Pronouns.mgr - Swedish-pack first/second-person pronouns (Phase 7).
;
; Possessive forms ("min" / "mitt" / "mina") are gender/number-inflected in
; Swedish (common / neuter / plural). v1 ships the common-gender form "min" /
; "din" only - all the kinship nouns the description corpus surfaces (mor /
; far / syster / bror / man / fru / son / dotter) are common gender, so this
; covers tell_about. Adding "mitt" / "mina" is a future morphology-engine
; job once adjective-agreement lands (see phase7_design.md open items).
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

:PRONOUN

"jag"    ?_I     .
"mig"    ?_I     .
"min"    ?_I     .

"du"     ?_you   .
"dig"    ?_you   .
"din"    ?_you   .

"den"    ?_this  .
"det"    ?_this  .

; Third-person pronouns. Same variables as en/Pronouns.mgr - one per gender and
; case. Swedish has
; distinct object forms (henne / honom / dem).

"hon"    ?_third_f
:: agree:f
.
"han"    ?_third_m
:: agree:m
.
"de"     ?_third_s  .

"henne"  ?_third_fo
:: agree:f
.
"honom"  ?_third_mo
:: agree:m
.
"dem"    ?_third_o  .
